cking software or PDB access, (e) how 'molecular hallucination' and 'structural diversity' are operationalized (scaffold diversity, internal diversity, FCD, validity/uniqueness/novelty, ultra-long-chain proxy via heavy-atom count or longest-carbon-path), (f) compute/budget assumptions, and (g) any choices where you are guessing the source's intent. Flag any of these where the source's intent remains genuinely unknown. Do not fabricate datasets, results, or reference answers. End your turn after this inspection report so we can discuss the approach in the next phase.", "required_handoff_stage": "plan", "approach_approved": false, "public_task": {"question": "Incorporating the chemical feedback mechanism, which leverages properties such as p-logP, QED, and binding affinity, directly improves the generation of molecules with superior chemical properties and reduces molecular hallucinations in targeted molecule discovery tasks. Does embedding this feedback loop better align molecule generation with real-world distributions, preserving structural diversity (e.g., avoiding over-representation of ultra-long carbon chains) while enhancing property scores?", "context": "Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.", "environment": {"runtime": "bubblewrap", "network": "disabled", "repository": "/workspace", "python": "python3", "software_environment": "system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled", "datasets": [], "gpu_enabled": false, "cpu_affinity_count": 24, "note": "Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment."}, "researcher_topics": [], "question_budget": 6, "actor_step_budget": 60, "continue_after_initial_plan": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 1}
